            <ArticleTitle>[Unexpected complication of anticoagulation after implantation of a coronary stent].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>180-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After stent implantation there is a high risk of acute stent thrombosis. Therefore, a very aggressive anticoagulation drug regimen is necessary. Two patients developed large hematomas of the upperarm that where presumably caused by automatic blood pressure measuring equipment or by a tourniquet used during blood collection. In one patient a complete paralysis of the ulnar and radial nerves resulted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
